From 860563cd7f2200ad403afcebcc74b4a1ca69270e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 22:35:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/36] Qt4 compat for post-v0.6 API additions

- QStringLiteral: force-include a one-line src/Common/Qt4Compat.h ahead
  of every translation unit on the Qt4 build (via -include in
  CMakeLists.txt) instead of touching its ~835 call sites.
- Drop the four v0.6-era #include "mimetypes-qt4/include/QMimeDatabase"
  guards that af84b80c's revert resurrected in ComposerAttachments.cpp,
  MessageComposer.cpp, AttachmentView.cpp and PartWalker_impl.h: the
  vendored backport is gone (see the cmake commit), and the plain
  #include <QMimeDatabase> already resolves against the external
  QtMimeTypes library on Qt4.
- Window.cpp: QGuiApplication::applicationStateChanged/applicationState()
  have no Qt4 equivalent; guard both behind QT_VERSION and fall back to
  always showing the network-error box right away (this is exactly
  what happened before this activation-aware behavior existed). Convert
  the QTimer::singleShot(250, lambda) hover-tooltip workaround (the
  singleShot-with-functor overload needs Qt 5.4) to a named slot pair
  with a pending-URL member instead, which works unchanged on Qt4.

The rest of the Phase-2 checklist (toHtmlEscaped, QUrlQuery,
QStandardPaths, setSectionResizeMode) was already dual-Qt-clean after
the af84b80c/e76c8774 revert commit -- verified by grep, no changes
needed there.
